<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Friday 95,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Friday 95,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said estimated interior</p>
<p>Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts were:</p>
<p>Friday:   95,000  Wk ago:  94,000  Yr ago: 100,000</p>
<p>Saturday: 15,000  Wk ago:  15,000  Yr ago:  27,000</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts mostly steady with the mid-session Thursday. Trade slow for moderate demand and light offerings.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    58.00 -59.00	   59.00 -60.00</p>
<p>few				 57.50		    58.50</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    57.00 -59.00	   57.50 -60.00</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    57.00 -59.00	   57.50 -60.00</p>
<p>Sows:  steady to 1.50 lower decline on 450 lbs down.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs.  44.00 -47.00	   45.00 -48.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   45.50 -47.00	   45.50 -48.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    46.00 -49.00	   47.00 -50.00</p>
<p>Compared to last week: Barrows and Gilts 1.00 higher. Sows mostly 1.00-2.00 higher.  Receipts this week 535,000 last week 514,000, last year 519,000. Barrows and Gilts average weight for week ending July 12, 1997  250.4 lbs compared to 250.9 lbs previous week 246.0 lbs last year.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
